            "guidance": "Install only if you trust LinkFox as the API, billing, and file-hosting provider. Keep gateway/login environment variables pointed at official LinkFox hosts, avoid uploading private reports unless a public URL is intended, review any phone/SMS or payment prompts carefully, and do not allow the self-extension workflow to add new skills without a separate review.",
            "findings": "[TT3] unexpected: Network use is expected for LinkFox APIs, but the artifact-backed concern is valid for sensitive flows: onboarding and gateway code can send Authorization headers, phone/SMS login data, token-generation traffic, and order actions to endpoints derived from environment variables without an allowlist.\n[TT3] expected: SERP, Keepa, text-generation, and upload network calls are part of the stated workflow; the risk is under-scoped endpoint configurability and broad URL fetching, not network access by itself.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill documentation discloses many operations, but there is no separate permission declaration for network, local persistence, public upload, account handling, or payment-related helper authority.\n[TP4] unexpected: The main market-analysis purpose is coherent, but the package also contains generic AIGC, feedback, account onboarding, API-key generation, and payment-order workflows that are broader than a user would expect from a SERP analyst skill.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The self-extension instruction to invoke expert-skill-creator and the account/payment onboarding materials materially expand trust boundaries beyond the reviewed SERP analysis behavior.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Automatic cross-skill orchestration is partly justified for report generation and image understanding, but downstream generation chaining, feedback submission, and payment/order helpers are not necessary for the core analysis task.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The artifact contains scope inconsistencies: helper docs discuss downstream generation while saying generation is out of scope, and storage docs say to avoid temp paths while implementations can fall back to home or temp directories.",
